<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!--
    The language algorithms library of the shared JavaScript libraries programme: number
    conversion, numerics, text, Date, the Temporal core and the time-zone algorithms, data-free,
    referencing the base class library only (architecture section 2).

    It holds the contract types of the conventions (the metering delegate, the status enumeration
    and the limit records) and, from milestone SJL-3, its first area: number conversion
    (Broiler.ECMAScript.Numbers) - Number::toString at every radix, toFixed, toExponential and
    toPrecision, StringToNumber, parseInt and parseFloat, numeric literal values, the array-index
    and canonical numeric key tests, and the StrWhiteSpaceChar set; from SJL-4, numerics in the same
    namespace; and from SJL-5, text (Broiler.ECMAScript.Text) - UTF-16, padding and relative indices,
    replacement templates, the URI, base64 and hex codecs, and JSON's grammar, quoting and gap; and
    from SJL-6, Date (Broiler.ECMAScript.Time) - the time-value arithmetic, the ISO calendar's
    civil-day helpers, the local-time provider with LocalTime and UTC, the Date string grammar in two
    dialects and the Date renderings; and from SJL-8, time zones and calendar years in the same
    namespace - the decoder of the data home's time-zone and calendar tables over the bytes an engine
    hands in, the zone algorithms over it, the offset time zones, and the table-backed calendars'
    years; and from SJL-10, the Temporal core (Broiler.ECMAScript.Temporal) - from part A of SJL-10.3,
    its records and limits, balancing, regulation and addition, grammar and serialization. It embeds no
    table. Its preview pre-releases reach Broiler.VM through that repository's
    committed feed (decision SJL-D-4 (c)).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Broiler.ECMAScript</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms</AssemblyName>
    <PackageId>Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms</PackageId>
    <Description>The language algorithms shared by the Broiler JavaScript engines: number conversion (Number::toString at every radix, toFixed, toExponential, toPrecision, StringToNumber, parseInt, parseFloat, numeric literal values, numeric keys and the string white-space set), numerics (the integer conversions, Float16, the Math kernels, exact rounding and the BigInt kernel) and text (UTF-16, padding and relative indices, replacement templates, the URI, base64 and hex codecs, and JSON's grammar, quoting and gap) and Date (the time-value arithmetic, the ISO calendar's civil-day helpers, the local-time provider with LocalTime and UTC, Date.parse's grammar in a strict and a Broiler.VM dialect, and the Date renderings) and time zones and calendar years (the decoder of the time-zone and calendar tables an engine hands in, lookup and primary identifiers, offsets and transitions with no 2037 cliff, possible instants, disambiguation, the start of a day, the offset time zones, and the Chinese, Korean, Umm al-Qura and Persian years) and the Temporal core's records and limits, balancing, regulation and addition, ISO 8601 / RFC 9557 grammar and string forms, with the WorkCharge metering delegate, the ResultStatus enumeration and the limit records every shared operation uses.</Description>
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The tests recompute the internal tables (ShortestDecimal's multipliers) and call the internal steps directly. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
